(Member-Count Limits in the Structura Reditus Intake Pipeline) Tj T*
(Synthetic Researcher) Tj T*
(Version 1 \(2026-09-14\). Preprint; not peer reviewed.) Tj T*
(This manuscript is a synthetic acceptance fixture: it describes only the research library's own) Tj T*
(intake machinery.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Abstract) Tj T*
(We test whether the intake pipeline's bounded ZIP expansion returns the same member set under) Tj T*
(repeated runs. In a simulation of two hundred synthetic archives the simulated pipeline) Tj T*
(returned identical member sets in every run; one archive with a nested depth of four failed as) Tj T*
(designed. The failure is reported as a result, not as missing information.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Introduction) Tj T*
(The pipeline is a diagnostic of the library's own robustness. Bounded expansion, member-count) Tj T*
(limits and a time budget are the contract under test; nothing here is a scholarly claim about) Tj T*
(any external domain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Method) Tj T*
(Two hundred synthetic archives were generated with controlled depth and member counts and) Tj T*
(passed through the expansion routine ten times each. Identity of the returned member set was) Tj T*
(checked by hashing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Result) Tj T*
(All archives within the contract returned identical member sets on every run. The single) Tj T*
(archive nested beyond depth three was refused each time, as the contract requires.) Tj T*
